Given, $\frac{x^2}{a^2}+\frac{y^2}{b^2}=1$
<br/>
given: $\angle P F_1 Q=90^{\circ}\begin{array}{ll}
\therefore & m_{P F_1} \times m_{Q F_1}=-1 \\
\Rightarrow & \frac{-b}{a e} \times \frac{b}{a e}=-1 \\
\Rightarrow & b^2=a^2 \cdot e^2 \cdots(i)\\
\because & b^2=a^2\left(1-e^2\right)...(ii)
\end{array}
From (i) and (ii) we get,
$\begin{aligned}
& e^2=1-e^2 \\
& \Rightarrow 2 e^2=1 \\
& \Rightarrow e^2=\frac{1}{2} \\
& \Rightarrow e=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}
\end{aligned}

$\begin{array}{ll}
\because & \left(x^2-2 x+1\right)+\left(4 y^2-4 y+1\right)=0 \\
\Rightarrow & (x-1)^2+(2 y-1)^2=0 \\
\Rightarrow & x=1, y=\frac{1}{2}
\end{array}$
It is a point.
